    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We present two datasets to evaluate asymmetric image comparisons, in the context of retrieval applications:\r\n  (i) Asym-QCD: this dataset considers the case where the query image is contained in a database image\r\n  (ii) Asym-DCQ: this dataset considers the case where a database image is contained in the query image\r\n\r\nThe images used in this dataset are collected from the Stanford Mobile Visual Search, INRIA Holidays and MIR-FLICKR datasets.\r\nInstructions are given (see README.txt file) for appropriate download and setup of dataset images.\r\n\r\nThe query images used in Asym-QCD are clean images of objects, and their corresponding correct database matches are images where the object is shown along with clutter.\r\nFor the Asym-DCQ dataset, these two sets of images are reversed: the database contains clean object images, and the queries are cluttered images.\r\nWe construct several versions of each of the two datasets, with different amounts of clutter:\r\n  (i) Asym-QCD: from 0 to 40 clutter images are added to each database item,\r\n  (ii) Asym-DCQ: from 0 to 40 clutter images are added to each query item.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Araujo, A. and Girod, B. Large-Scale Video Retrieval Using Image Queries. (2017). IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology. https://dx.doi.org/10.1109/TCSVT.2017.2667710.",
